(;FF[4]CA[UTF-8]GM[1]SZ[19]GN[Type 3 Black Go Immortal

There is one more sunspot than the previous type, and White firstLower and Black Go are also alive.

There is a saying that "six deaths and eight lives" must not be forgotten.

johny's note: Isn't it "Seven die but eight live"? My understanding is this. When the upper line of the second line is tied with six black stones, Black first will not live; when there are eight black stones tied, White first will not die.
So it's "six deaths and eight lives." When there are seven sunspots in a row, Black lives, White first (Black) dies. Of course, as the transformation of this type points out, when there are no white stones on either side of the seven black stones, the White first black will not die.]GC[Type: Appreciation question | Level: 5K | Rating: 4.4/5 | Correct: 36% (5/14) | Desc: Type 3 Black Go Immortal

